Track 3: The Secondhand Skips a Beat
- Story & Context: Legend says this closing track was mixed live during the final sunrise at the ruined Estufa-Verde venue right before police bulldozers demolished the site. As the machinery idle hummed outside, producer Dra. Beatriz Vane muted the sub-bass completely, leaving only a bone-chilling piccolo solo echoing through the shattered glass dome over a faint, erratic tamborzão clap. The crowd remained totally silent, listening to the final decaying tail of reverb as the plant bio-sensors flatlined on screen, prompting a vocal sample from a spectator to cut the air: "Listen close, it leaves no shadow behind."  
